# .cto/devteam-model — the model ORCHESTRATED windows run on.
#
# Copy to `.cto/devteam-model` to change it. With no file you get `default`, which
# is what you want if the answer is "whatever Anthropic currently defaults to".
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS: Claude Code's /model picker changes the window you type it
# in AND saves the choice as the machine-global default for every session started
# afterwards. A launcher that passes no model inherits that — which is how a Fable
# pick in a CTO window ended up running three dev tabs on 2026-09-02 (see
# docs/memos/2026-09-03-rca-handoff-model-inheritance.md). `claude --model X` is
# scoped to the session it launches and writes nothing back, so pinning here means
# the CEO can pick freely in the CTO window without it reaching the fleet.
#
# Consumed by scripts/cto/resolve-devteam-model.sh, which /handoff,
# /resume-dev-team and qa-drive-claude.sh all resolve through.
# Precedence: DEVTEAM_MODEL env var > this file > built-in `default`.

# ── the fleet default: first bare line wins ──────────────────────────────────
#
# default   — RECOMMENDED, and the built-in. Resolves at launch to the ACCOUNT
#             default, so it follows Anthropic as they move it (context variants
#             included — today that is Opus 5 with 1M). Being a CLI flag, it is
#             NOT the machine-global default a /model pick rewrites. Tracking
#             Anthropic and isolation from /model are usually wanted together;
#             this is the only value that gives both.
#
# opus      — an ALIAS. Use when the fleet should sit on a specific FAMILY no
# sonnet      matter what Anthropic defaults to. Tracks the latest model of that
# haiku       family so it never stales, but may not select a context variant
# fable       (plain `opus` is not the 1M build).
#
# claude-opus-5[1m]
#           — a full name. Only when you need one exact build. Ages into a
#             retired model with nobody editing the line; revisit each release.
#
# inherit   — take the machine-global default; no --model flag. This is the
#             pre-2026-09-03 behaviour and it is NOT "the account default": the
#             two coincide only until someone runs /model, after which the fleet
#             follows that pick. If you want "whatever Anthropic defaults to",
#             the value is `default`, not this.

default

# ── optional per-repo overrides, one per line ────────────────────────────────
#   acme-tuner=fable
#   acme-demo-app=sonnet
